{
  "version": 1,
  "note": "Twelve verified Google Fonts pairings for landing pages; the agent picks one by matching the brand brief to a suits line and passes its id to brand_tokens.py --pairing, which writes the stacks, the dials and the metric-matched fallbacks into the token block and the url into an @import at the top of global.css - everything here except bodyLineHeight, which has no token and is set by hand on body. Each role carries its OWN fallback, and each fallback states size-adjust per font-weight: every brand renders headings at 700, a real face gets wider at 700, and a local Arial thickened synthetically does not - so one figure solved at 400 makes the fallback narrower than the webfont at every heading and the block meant to stop the reflow causes one. The size-adjust figures are solved empirically in Chromium against Arial; ascent, descent and line-gap are the real face's own metrics and do not vary with weight.",
